{"2476430": {"success": true, "data": {"type": "game", "name": "Grimoire Limbo", "steam_appid": 2476430, "required_age": 0, "is_free": false, "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong><i>Trapped in a Necromancer's Grimoire, can you find your memories and escape before losing your mind?</i></strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Grimoire Limbo is a turn-based horror roguelite set in beautifully crafted, etched-ink environments. 2D sprites interact with the 3D-world like drawings in a book. Every encounter wears on your sanity. Recover a lost memory, and you pull back from the edge. Die, and you slide closer to it.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >You can only keep what you can carry - two weapons and two utility items. Every use damages the item a little more until it breaks. Keep the trusted weapon that's almost spent and risk it failing mid-fight, or replace it with one that might not be as powerful but will last a little longer.</p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Turn-based combat</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >An etched-ink world where 2D figures move through the 3D world</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Scarcity-driven load-out management</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Constant Sanity pressure. Recover lost memories to hold back the dark. See the world change as Sanity slides.</p></li></ul>", "about_the_game": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong><i>Trapped in a Necromancer's Grimoire, can you find your memories and escape before losing your mind?</i></strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Grimoire Limbo is a turn-based horror roguelite set in beautifully crafted, etched-ink environments. 2D sprites interact with the 3D-world like drawings in a book. Every encounter wears on your sanity. Recover a lost memory, and you pull back from the edge. Die, and you slide closer to it.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >You can only keep what you can carry - two weapons and two utility items. Every use damages the item a little more until it breaks. Keep the trusted weapon that's almost spent and risk it failing mid-fight, or replace it with one that might not be as powerful but will last a little longer.</p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Turn-based combat</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >An etched-ink world where 2D figures move through the 3D world</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Scarcity-driven load-out management</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Constant Sanity pressure. Recover lost memories to hold back the dark. See the world change as Sanity slides.</p></li></ul>", "short_description": "Grimoire Limbo traps you in a necromancer's grimoire with no idea how you got there. Explore an eerie world to find your memories as your sanity frays and warps what you see. Fight with turn-based combat and spend crystals to grow stronger or secure your progress.", "supported_languages": "English<strong>*</strong><br><strong>*</strong>languages with full audio support", "header_image": "https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2476430/b6920b00ca3d48bc280345d32cf0969705f28e93/header.jpg?t=1785937613", "capsule_image": "https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2476430/de5cb12f5e2d641d693446aaa22491c5cdc5db42/capsule_231x87.jpg?t=1785937613", "capsule_imagev5": "https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2476430/de5cb12f5e2d641d693446aaa22491c5cdc5db42/capsule_184x69.jpg?t=1785937613", "website": "https://infiniteloom.games/games/grimoire-limbo", "pc_requirements": {"minimum": "<strong>Minimum:</strong><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li>Requires a 64-bit processor and operating system<br></li><li><strong>OS:</strong> 10<br></li><li><strong>Processor:</strong> i5<br></li><li><strong>Memory:</strong> 8 GB RAM<br></li><li><strong>Graphics:</strong> nVidia GTX 2060<br></li><li><strong>DirectX:</strong> Version 11<br></li><li><strong>Storage:</strong> 1 GB available space<br></li><li><strong>Sou